# Drive one mate closed under uncertainty (ARCHITECTURE_SEAMS.md 2026-10-19). The driver reads the assembly
# graph itself (closing path, acceptance, symmetry) and derives stages and clearances from CAD; nothing here names
# a part's constants. Certification is NOT this action's: ExecuteMate (pa_assembly_msgs) certifies afterwards.
#
# mate_id  assembly-qualified mate, e.g. "fmb1/mate:00" (the assembly graph's mate address)
# target   the observed pose of the mate's parent (the base, or the seated part it goes into)
# held     the held part's pose in the gripper (tool) frame, measured once per grasp
# corrections_json  the planner's aim corrections (seams.aim.corrections_json: follow / bias / yaw_exp), applied by the
#          driver on the base its own alignment arrives at (2026-10-22, AR3: vision measures, drive-mate moves)
string mate_id
fmb_seam_msgs/VisionPose target
fmb_seam_msgs/VisionPose held
string corrections_json
---
bool seated                         # the driver's own end-state claim (raw-trace based); ExecuteMate decides
string stage_reached                # SEAT | BASE_RIM | OBJ:<part> | WEDGED | NONE - from the trace vs the CAD contact heights
float64[2] slide                    # x/y travel of the held part from first contact to the end (m, base frame)
string trace_path                   # raw telemetry of the attempt(s)
float64[3] measured_correction      # where the part ended vs the commanded target (m, base frame)
string refusal                      # why it did not try / stopped, by name; empty if it ran
fmb_seam_msgs/VisionPose base_measured   # the base as the driver last measured it (its alignment's read; the planner
                                    # aims the next insert from it, never from this insert's aim)
string align_json                   # the alignment: route, measured, log, aim, corrections applied
---
string stage
float64 z_above_seat
